What is the median number of books read?', NULL, $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"$2$"},{"key":"B","text":"$3$"},{"key":"C","text":"$3.5$"},{"key":"D","text":"$4$"}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'B', NULL, E'With 21 data values, the median is the 11th value when the data are arranged in order. The cumulative frequencies are: 1 book (3 students, cumulative 3), 2 books (7 students, cumulative 10), 3 books (4 students, cumulative 14). Since the 11th value falls in the group that read 3 books (cumulative positions 11 through 14), the median is $3$. The value $2$ is the mode (highest frequency of 7) but not the median. The value $3.5$ incorrectly averages 3 and 4 as if the median fell between two groups. The value $4$ results from counting from the wrong end of the distribution.', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"concept_gap"},"B":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"C":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"arithmetic_slip"},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"misread_question"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 75, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-10-18"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-10-18","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);

















